cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "deberka-jordan: reallocation plans for a shared resource by the Hahn-Jordan decomposition"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for reallocation cycles of a shared resource as signed
  measures: the Hahn and Jordan decompositions, the least-volume netting of
  proposals, a safe two-phase order that never overdraws the pool, an executor
  that waits for freed memory, the oscillation index and the dead-band choice
  on demand traces, and a libvirt balloon backend for KVM virtual machines.
